1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:00,783
Own stock tokens

2
00:00:00,833 --> 00:00:02,211
that just sit in your wallet?

3
00:00:02,261 --> 00:00:03,838
What if they earned income every week,

4
00:00:03,888 --> 00:00:05,486
under rules the agent can't break?

5
00:00:05,536 --> 00:00:06,704
That's Strike.

6
00:00:06,784 --> 00:00:08,798
Wall Street holders sell
covered calls for income,

7
00:00:08,848 --> 00:00:10,708
but someone must pick each week's strike,

8
00:00:10,758 --> 00:00:12,144
and you must trust them.

9
00:00:12,194 --> 00:00:13,275
On-chain it's harder:

10
00:00:13,325 --> 00:00:15,061
multipliers easy to apply twice,

11
00:00:15,112 --> 00:00:16,182
weekend price freezes,

12
00:00:16,232 --> 00:00:17,860
pauses, mid-week splits.

13
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:19,246
So tokens sit idle,

14
00:00:19,297 --> 00:00:21,109
or go to managers nobody can check.

15
00:00:21,159 --> 00:00:23,328
In Strike, an agent picks
the strike each week,

16
00:00:23,378 --> 00:00:24,820
held to the rules by a contract.

17
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:26,676
Options vaults for stock tokens.

18
00:00:26,726 --> 00:00:28,866
Weekly premium in USDG.

19
00:00:28,916 --> 00:00:31,343
An AI agent picks the
strike, inside a mandate.

20
00:00:31,393 --> 00:00:33,533
Break it, and its bond goes to depositors.

21
00:00:33,583 --> 00:00:35,081
Rust on Stylus does the math.

22
00:00:35,131 --> 00:00:37,875
Live on Robinhood Chain
and Arbitrum Sepolia.

23
00:00:37,925 --> 00:00:38,801
Inside one week:

24
00:00:38,851 --> 00:00:40,922
Depositors fill a vault
with a fixed mandate.

25
00:00:40,972 --> 00:00:43,369
An agent reads it via MCP and dry-runs.

26
00:00:43,419 --> 00:00:46,033
It proposes delta, expiry, size and price.

27
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:48,697
The Epoch Manager checks it
at guarded oracle prices.

28
00:00:48,747 --> 00:00:51,153
Rust on Stylus solves and
stress-tests the strike.

29
00:00:51,203 --> 00:00:53,916
If it passes, buyers pay premium in USDG.

30
00:00:53,966 --> 00:00:56,175
If not, the bond is slashed to depositors.

31
00:00:56,225 --> 00:00:57,669
Decisions are hashed on-chain;

32
00:00:57,719 --> 00:01:00,261
the agent has an ERC-8004 identity.

33
00:01:00,311 --> 00:01:01,349
Friday's close settles;

34
00:01:01,399 --> 00:01:03,261
depositors get the premium, less a fee.

35
00:01:03,311 --> 00:01:06,322
Same contracts on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum Sepolia.

36
00:01:06,372 --> 00:01:07,940
Say Maya opens the Tesla vault.

37
00:01:07,990 --> 00:01:11,620
Its first week sold the $369.86 call:

38
00:01:11,670 --> 00:01:13,646
four options, 10.01 USDG.

39
00:01:13,696 --> 00:01:15,668
At or below the strike, Maya keeps it;

40
00:01:15,718 --> 00:01:18,939
the buyer profits above $372.36.

41
00:01:18,989 --> 00:01:20,386
The limits are in the contract:

42
00:01:20,436 --> 00:01:22,749
Delta 0.10 to 0.35,

43
00:01:22,799 --> 00:01:24,605
at least 95% of fair value,

44
00:01:24,655 --> 00:01:26,715
at least 0.05% yield,

45
00:01:26,765 --> 00:01:28,118
at most 80% sold,

46
00:01:28,168 --> 00:01:29,217
1 to 8 days,

47
00:01:29,267 --> 00:01:30,240
fixed for good.

48
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:31,867
The playground tests a proposal live,

49
00:01:31,917 --> 00:01:32,578
no wallet.

50
00:01:32,628 --> 00:01:35,084
An honest 0.20-delta call: accepted.

51
00:01:35,134 --> 00:01:36,476
A reckless at-the-money strike:

52
00:01:36,526 --> 00:01:38,084
rejected, delta out of band.

53
00:01:38,134 --> 00:01:41,708
A real one costs the agent
10 USDG, paid to depositors.

54
00:01:41,758 --> 00:01:44,716
Run the agent does the rule
stages live, in your browser,

55
00:01:44,766 --> 00:01:47,183
against the real vault, sending nothing.

56
00:01:47,358 --> 00:01:48,775
Buyers pay at the moment they buy:

57
00:01:48,825 --> 00:01:51,516
oracle spot moved 0.5% against them,

58
00:01:51,566 --> 00:01:53,616
Black-Scholes, times the agent's factor.

59
00:01:53,666 --> 00:01:55,040
Never below intrinsic value,

60
00:01:55,090 --> 00:01:56,883
so stale prices can't be picked off.

61
00:01:56,933 --> 00:01:58,358
Buying waits for the NYSE open,

62
00:01:58,408 --> 00:01:59,924
shown in your own time zone.

63
00:01:59,974 --> 00:02:03,375
Live on September 29, the seller
agent asked for 0.20 delta;

64
00:02:03,425 --> 00:02:07,121
the contract solved $369.86, accepted.

65
00:02:07,171 --> 00:02:09,390
A reckless agent forced
an at-the-money put:

66
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:11,657
rejected, 10 USDG slashed,

67
00:02:11,707 --> 00:02:13,389
bond 60 to 50.

68
00:02:13,439 --> 00:02:16,461
The explorer says Success:
a rejection isn't a revert,

69
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,386
and 10 USDG left the bond.

70
00:02:18,436 --> 00:02:21,106
The call expired Friday at 20:00 UTC;

71
00:02:21,156 --> 00:02:22,167
it has not settled yet.

72
00:02:22,217 --> 00:02:24,850
It settles at the first mainnet
Chainlink print after expiry;

73
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:26,570
the contract rejects any other price.

74
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:29,669
The last print, at 19:55,
came before expiry.

75
00:02:29,719 --> 00:02:32,053
The epoch trace shows
each step's transaction,

76
00:02:32,103 --> 00:02:33,174
and what is pending.

77
00:02:33,224 --> 00:02:35,191
Anyone can run an agent,
with no permission.

78
00:02:35,241 --> 00:02:37,109
Here a test wallet registers an agent

79
00:02:37,159 --> 00:02:39,732
and bonds 60 USDG, above the 50 minimum.

80
00:02:39,782 --> 00:02:40,751
The wallet signs each step:

81
00:02:40,801 --> 00:02:41,991
register, then bond.

82
00:02:42,041 --> 00:02:44,972
Each one waits for its block
on Robinhood Chain testnet.

83
00:02:45,172 --> 00:02:46,114
Now it can propose.

84
00:02:46,164 --> 00:02:49,253
Every rejected proposal costs it 10 USDG.

85
00:02:54,124 --> 00:02:56,058
On Arbitrum Sepolia, Claude planned it:

86
00:02:56,108 --> 00:02:58,460
via Strike's MCP server, it read the vault

87
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:00,056
and dry-ran five candidates.

88
00:03:00,106 --> 00:03:04,030
It chose 0.20 delta at 105% of fair value,

89
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:04,638
and wrote why:

90
00:03:04,688 --> 00:03:06,078
mid-band, safe from small moves.

91
00:03:06,128 --> 00:03:09,870
The contract solved $364.29: accepted.

92
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:10,729
On Arbiscan:

93
00:03:10,779 --> 00:03:12,643
a successful call from the agent's signer.

94
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:15,182
The same run slashed a
reckless put 10 USDG,

95
00:03:15,232 --> 00:03:16,780
and a buyer took all 4 calls.

96
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:17,706
In 3D:

97
00:03:17,756 --> 00:03:20,554
Across, Tesla's price. Back, days left.

98
00:03:20,604 --> 00:03:21,881
Up, a share's value.

99
00:03:21,931 --> 00:03:25,620
At expiry it bends flat
at the $364.29 strike:

100
00:03:25,670 --> 00:03:26,886
upside goes to the buyer.

101
00:03:26,936 --> 00:03:30,500
Below, the depositor keeps
stock plus $2.23 per option.

102
00:03:30,550 --> 00:03:32,878
The math is Rust, on Arbitrum Stylus.

103
00:03:32,928 --> 00:03:35,518
Solving a strike takes
48 Black-Scholes runs:

104
00:03:35,568 --> 00:03:37,806
6.5 times less gas than Solidity,

105
00:03:37,856 --> 00:03:39,968
3.3 times less per proposal.

106
00:03:40,018 --> 00:03:41,615
Every run leaves a decision record.

107
00:03:41,665 --> 00:03:43,562
Its hash is anchored in the DecisionLog;

108
00:03:43,612 --> 00:03:45,593
rehash the file, and it matches the chain.

109
00:03:45,643 --> 00:03:47,556
CI re-checks every cited transaction:

110
00:03:47,606 --> 00:03:50,689
177 of 177 verified.

111
00:03:50,739 --> 00:03:52,300
The agent now runs five stages:

112
00:03:52,350 --> 00:03:55,566
market, risk, strike planner,
critic, then the contract.

113
00:03:55,616 --> 00:03:58,409
In this Claude-planned dry run,
four passed and nothing was sent;

114
00:03:58,459 --> 00:03:59,960
its token use is on record.

115
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:02,270
On the weekend, the market
analyst said no trade;

116
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,584
the rest never ran.

117
00:04:03,634 --> 00:04:05,067
Agent two's accepted put:

118
00:04:05,117 --> 00:04:07,128
each mandate rule, with the headroom left.

119
00:04:07,178 --> 00:04:08,174
Why not the other strikes:

120
00:04:08,224 --> 00:04:10,997
the same proposal at each
delta, judged by the rules.

121
00:04:11,047 --> 00:04:12,240
What would make the week lose:

122
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:15,829
TSLA below $340.20, 17% model odds,

123
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:17,653
then stress rows and what-ifs.

124
00:04:17,703 --> 00:04:19,279
Agent one's forced put was rejected:

125
00:04:19,330 --> 00:04:22,284
the check stops at the delta
band; later rules never run.

126
00:04:22,334 --> 00:04:24,263
Its ERC-8004 identity:

127
00:04:24,313 --> 00:04:28,426
114 on Robinhood Chain testnet,
253 on Arbitrum Sepolia.

128
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:29,002
The monitor,

129
00:04:29,052 --> 00:04:29,915
live on mainnet:

130
00:04:29,965 --> 00:04:34,801
Nvidia's multiplier, 1.000775,
is already in the price,

131
00:04:34,851 --> 00:04:36,749
so Strike never applies it twice.

132
00:04:36,799 --> 00:04:39,208
Over 403 weeks since 2019,

133
00:04:39,258 --> 00:04:42,494
covered calls cut volatility 25 to 46%,

134
00:04:42,544 --> 00:04:43,982
but lagged holding everywhere:

135
00:04:44,032 --> 00:04:47,993
Tesla 23.1% a year, against 44.0% held.

136
00:04:48,043 --> 00:04:49,829
And it assumes full weekly sales.

137
00:04:49,879 --> 00:04:50,943
The proof page:

138
00:04:50,993 --> 00:04:53,151
1,607 tests and proofs,

139
00:04:53,201 --> 00:04:54,900
99.3% line coverage,

140
00:04:54,951 --> 00:04:56,020
nine Halmos proofs,

141
00:04:56,071 --> 00:04:57,785
all 11 review findings fixed.

142
00:04:57,835 --> 00:04:59,422
Running by itself reads both testnets:

143
00:04:59,472 --> 00:05:00,761
prices, each vault's week,

144
00:05:00,811 --> 00:05:01,763
the scheduled jobs.

145
00:05:01,813 --> 00:05:03,677
The mirror audit checks
every copied price:

146
00:05:03,727 --> 00:05:06,681
84 of 84 rounds match mainnet Chainlink.

147
00:05:06,731 --> 00:05:08,169
9 lessons from the live runs,

148
00:05:08,219 --> 00:05:10,571
each with evidence, the fix and its test.

149
00:05:10,621 --> 00:05:11,507
Who else is here?

150
00:05:11,557 --> 00:05:14,419
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets on
Robinhood Chain are order books:

151
00:05:14,469 --> 00:05:15,988
traders pick strike and price.

152
00:05:16,038 --> 00:05:18,473
Ribbon, Derive and Thetanuts
sell crypto options

153
00:05:18,523 --> 00:05:20,213
by auction, order book or RFQ.

154
00:05:20,263 --> 00:05:22,586
Tilt's AI manages vaults, with no options;

155
00:05:22,636 --> 00:05:25,131
its sources don't say
what limits it on-chain.

156
00:05:25,181 --> 00:05:26,923
In Strike, a bonded agent proposes,

157
00:05:26,973 --> 00:05:28,725
the contract enforces mandate and price,

158
00:05:28,775 --> 00:05:29,899
and rule-breakers pay.

159
00:05:29,949 --> 00:05:31,991
Stock-token traps are handled on-chain.

160
00:05:32,041 --> 00:05:34,094
Holders get income and keep their keys.

161
00:05:34,144 --> 00:05:36,946
Weekend freezes: settle on
the first post-expiry price.

162
00:05:36,996 --> 00:05:39,650
Multiplier: never applied, fork-tested.

163
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:42,344
Agent trust: fixed
mandate, bond, slashing.

164
00:05:42,394 --> 00:05:45,255
Gas: Rust on Stylus, 6.5 times cheaper.

165
00:05:45,305 --> 00:05:47,733
Not done: no audit, and testnet only.

166
00:05:47,783 --> 00:05:50,042
Next: eight settled
weeks, an external audit,

167
00:05:50,093 --> 00:05:51,732
then one capped mainnet vault.

168
00:05:51,782 --> 00:05:54,281
Strike: options on Robinhood
Chain and Arbitrum,

169
00:05:54,331 --> 00:05:56,357
run by agents held to a mandate.
